<main id="main">

<section class="bq-hero"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1759646827844-bbbdbfd0ada2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&h=760&q=75" alt="formal dining table set for a banquet" width="1600" height="760" fetchpriority="high"><div class="bq-w"><div class="bq-inv"><p class="bq-k">You are invited to host</p><h1>A generous table, beautifully set.</h1><p class="bq-lead">Banquet is an independent guide to hosting dinner for many: setting a formal table, planning seating for a crowd and timing a menu of several courses so every plate arrives at its best.</p><p class="bq-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Plan my dinner</a><a class="bq-ln" href="table-setting-guide.html">How to set a table</a></p></div></div></section>

<section class="bq-s"><div class="bq-w"><div class="bq-ttl"><span>&#10022;</span><h2>The order of the evening</h2><span>&#10022;</span></div><ol class="bq-courses"><li><i>I</i><b>Welcome</b><span>Small bites as guests arrive</span></li><li><i>II</i><b>Starter</b><span>Soup, salad or something light</span></li><li><i>III</i><b>Main</b><span>The centrepiece, served generously</span></li><li><i>IV</i><b>Cheese or salad</b><span>An optional pause</span></li><li><i>V</i><b>Dessert</b><span>Something sweet</span></li><li><i>VI</i><b>Coffee &amp; tea</b><span>With small treats</span></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="bq-s bq-iv"><div class="bq-w bq-ps"><div><p class="bq-k">Place setting</p><h2>Set from the outside in</h2><p class="bq-lead">A formal setting looks complicated, but it follows one simple rule: guests use cutlery from the outside towards the plate.</p><svg class="bq-diag" viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="Diagram of a formal place setting"><circle cx="210" cy="130" r="62" fill="#fff" stroke="#14213D" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="210" cy="130" r="42" fill="none" stroke="#C9A227" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="104" y="72" width="8" height="118" rx="4" fill="#14213D"/><rect x="122" y="72" width="8" height="118" rx="4" fill="#14213D"/><rect x="290" y="72" width="8" height="118" rx="4" fill="#C9A227"/><rect x="308" y="72" width="8" height="118" rx="4" fill="#C9A227"/><rect x="326" y="72" width="8" height="118" rx="4" fill="#8B6E2E"/><circle cx="118" cy="40" r="20" fill="#fff" stroke="#14213D" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="312" cy="36" r="13" fill="none" stroke="#14213D" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="340" cy="44" r="11" fill="none" stroke="#14213D" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="186" y="44" width="48" height="7" rx="3.5" fill="#8B6E2E"/><text x="117" y="214" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14213D">forks</text><text x="312" y="214" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14213D">knives &amp; spoon</text><text x="118" y="14" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14213D">bread</text><text x="326" y="14" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14213D">glasses</text><text x="210" y="34" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14213D">dessert</text></svg></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1772404245181-3701c768fe06?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=620&q=75" alt="formal table setting with floral arrangements" width="520" height="620" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

<section class="bq-tl" id="tools"><div class="bq-w"><div class="bq-ttl bq-ttl-w"><span>&#10022;</span><h2>Hosting tools</h2><span>&#10022;</span></div><div class="bq-menu">
<div class="bq-panel"><h3>Seating Planner</h3><p class="bq-pd">How many tables, and who sits where.</p><label for="sp-g">Guests<input id="sp-g" type="number" min="2" max="300" value="24"></label><label for="sp-t">Table shape<select id="sp-t"><option value="round8">Round, seats 8</option><option value="round10" selected>Round, seats 10</option><option value="long">Long tables, seats 12</option><option value="one">One long banquet table</option></select></label><div class="bq-out" id="sp-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="bq-panel"><h3>Place Setting Builder</h3><p class="bq-pd">Tick the courses you are serving.</p><div class="bq-ck" id="pb-c"><label><input type="checkbox" value="soup" checked> Soup</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="fish"> Fish course</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="starter" checked> Starter or salad</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="main" checked disabled> Main course</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="dessert" checked> Dessert</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="bread" checked> Bread</label></div><div class="bq-out" id="pb-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="bq-panel"><h3>Course Timing Planner</h3><p class="bq-pd">When each course should reach the table.</p><label for="ct-t">Guests sit down at<input id="ct-t" type="time" value="19:30"></label><label for="ct-n">Number of courses<select id="ct-n"><option value="3">Three</option><option value="4" selected>Four</option><option value="5">Five</option></select></label><div class="bq-out" id="ct-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="bq-s"><div class="bq-w bq-seat"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1763429338698-439aa108e7fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=640&q=75" alt="event hall with tables set for a banquet" width="560" height="640" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="bq-k">Seating</p><h2>The art of the seating plan</h2><ul class="bq-list"><li>Seat each guest beside someone they know and someone new.</li><li>Place lively conversationalists at the ends and in the middle.</li><li>Keep couples near each other but not side by side at long tables.</li><li>Seat guests with mobility needs near the door and the host.</li><li>Use place cards: they remove awkward hovering.</li></ul></div></div></section>

<section class="bq-trio"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585742440646-60adcd5a06d0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=420&q=75" alt="white and gold chandelier" width="520" height="420" loading="lazy"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794388558089-44b16b3a8f97?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=420&q=75" alt="yellow pillar candles glowing in glass" width="520" height="420" loading="lazy"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769812343531-cfe6bc93905e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=420&q=75" alt="table setting with white flowers" width="520" height="420" loading="lazy"></section>

<section class="bq-s"><div class="bq-w"><div class="bq-ttl"><span>&#10022;</span><h2>The guides</h2><span>&#10022;</span></div><div class="bq-gds"><a href="table-setting-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511795409834-ef04bbd61622?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="elegant table setting with a floral centrepiece" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"><div><p class="bq-k">Guide one</p><h3>The Table Setting Guide</h3><p>Informal, semi-formal and formal settings, glassware, napkins and centrepieces.</p></div></a><a href="hosting-large-dinner-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1783818412534-370b60b8a1d8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="long dining table with floral centrepieces" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"><div><p class="bq-k">Guide two</p><h3>The Hosting a Large Dinner Guide</h3><p>Planning, quantities, timing and service for twelve guests or a hundred.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="bq-s bq-iv"><div class="bq-w bq-fq"><div><div class="bq-ttl bq-ttl-l"><h2>Questions from hosts</h2></div><p class="bq-lead">Answers to what we are asked most.</p></div><div class="bq-faq"><details open><summary>How much space does each guest need at the table?</summary><p>Allow about 60 cm (24 in) of table edge per person for comfortable dining, and a little more for formal place settings with several glasses and pieces of cutlery.</p></details><details><summary>Which side does the bread plate go on?</summary><p>On the left, above the forks. Drinks go on the right, above the knives. An easy memory trick: make an &ldquo;b&rdquo; with your left hand (bread) and a &ldquo;d&rdquo; with your right (drink).</p></details><details><summary>In what order is cutlery used?</summary><p>From the outside in. The pieces furthest from the plate are for the first course, and you work towards the plate with each course.</p></details><details><summary>How do I seat a large group?</summary><p>Mix people so each guest sits near someone they know and someone new. Place the most outgoing guests at the ends and in the middle to keep conversation flowing.</p></details><details><summary>How long should a multi-course dinner take?</summary><p>Allow about 20&ndash;30 minutes for each lighter course and 40&ndash;45 minutes for the main, with short breaks between. A four-course dinner usually runs two to three hours.</p></details><details><summary>Round or long tables?</summary><p>Round tables make conversation easy across the whole table and suit groups of 6&ndash;10. Long tables feel grand and seat more people, but guests mostly talk to their neighbours.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="bq-nl"><div class="bq-w"><div class="bq-nl-c"><p class="bq-k">By invitation</p><h2>The Banquet Card</h2><p>One hosting idea and one table-setting tip, delivered monthly.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@banquet.com?subject=The%20Banquet%20Card&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></div></section>

